## 3. Noncommercial Use

You may use the Software for Noncommercial Use without payment and without
obtaining a separate license.

Examples include personal projects, hobbies, experimentation, research,
self-education, unpaid community activities, and ordinary noncommercial
educational use.

Legal form does not determine whether a use is Commercial Use. A nonprofit,
foundation, school, university, public institution, or similar Entity is subject
to the same rules as any other Entity.

## 4. Free Commercial Use Below the Revenue Threshold

You may use the Software for Commercial Use without obtaining a separate
commercial license if the combined Revenue of You and all Entities treated as a
single Entity under this License did not exceed the Revenue Threshold during the
Previous Financial Year.

The Revenue Threshold is:

**EUR 25,000 in gross Revenue during the Previous Financial Year.**

The nature or size of a particular contract, customer, project, or transaction
does not change this rule. For example, an eligible freelancer or microbusiness
may use the Software while performing work for a larger customer, provided that
the freelancer or microbusiness itself remains eligible under this Section.

Eligibility for a financial year is determined by reference to the Previous
Financial Year. Exceeding EUR 25,000 during the current financial year does not
automatically terminate eligibility during that same financial year.

If Revenue during a financial year exceeds the Revenue Threshold, a separate
commercial license is required for Commercial Use in the following financial
year.

## 5. New Entities

If an Entity has not yet completed a financial year, it may use the Software
under Section 4 if it reasonably and in good faith expects its Revenue during
its first financial year not to exceed the Revenue Threshold.

If that expectation is no longer reasonable, the Entity must obtain a separate
commercial license before continuing Commercial Use.

## 6. Commercial Use Above the Revenue Threshold

If You do not qualify under Section 4 or Section 5, this License does not permit
Commercial Use of the Software except where a specific exception in this
License applies.

You must obtain a separate commercial license from the Licensor before
continuing such Commercial Use.

The Licensor may offer commercial licenses on individually agreed terms,
including discounted or no-fee licenses. The Licensor is not obligated to offer
the same terms to different licensees.

Commercial licensing inquiries may be sent to:

**Damian Szczech**  
**szczech.dam+ewpwaveform@gmail.com**

## 7. Educational Use

Ordinary Noncommercial educational use is permitted without payment regardless
of the Revenue of the school, institution, teacher, or other Entity involved.

Examples include using the Software:

- as part of a lesson in a school or other educational institution;
- in a free course or workshop; or
- for demonstration, research, or teaching that is not itself a Commercial Use.

Use of the Software as part of a paid course, paid training program, paid
workshop, monetized educational product, or other Commercial Use is subject to
the Revenue Threshold unless the Tutorial Exception in Section 8 applies.

Educational institutions and other Entities may contact the Licensor to request
a discounted or no-fee commercial license.

## 8. Tutorial Exception

You may use the Software without obtaining a separate commercial license to
create, publish, sell, or monetize a tutorial, course, article, video, stream,
book, workshop, or similar educational material whose primary subject is how to
use `ewp-waveform`, even if Your Revenue exceeds the Revenue Threshold.

This exception applies only when `ewp-waveform` is the sole software product
being taught or is clearly the principal software product that is the subject of
the material.

This exception permits demonstration and use of the Software for the purpose of
teaching the Software. It does not permit:

- selling or commercially distributing the Software or a Modified Version;
- bundling the Software or a Modified Version as a paid component of the
  educational material;
- using the Software merely as one tool among several in a broader paid course
  where `ewp-waveform` is not the principal subject; or
- representing the educational material as endorsed, certified, or officially
  produced by the Licensor without permission.

